 was handed. E7 lost 15.6 points, dropping Black from +5.3 to -10.2; the engine's choice was H5. The chance to use the wall on the fourth line was gone in one move."}, {"turn": 28, "text": "F9 by the 20k lost 14.9 points, yet Black was still at -11.2 afterward. GPT-6.1 Sol answered with E9, which lost 12.9 points, and the gap went back to -24.2. Neither side was reading the top edge cleanly."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The inspect/audit function (stored via `store('inspect', ...)` and called as auditfn) only parses the board text, computes chains, liberties, empty regions and the captures of the single move the player already named, and the other commands only read files, replay the move list against the final board, compute a stored point-set history, and write notes and an SGF. Nothing loops over empty points to score candidates or plays continuations forward, so all of it works on the current position or on records.", "stop": false}}